When a ConvolverNode’s AudioNode is collected while it still has a tail
to play, Ladybird keeps rendering that tail and removes the render node
only once the tail has played out. The other engines likewise keep a
convolver active until its tail ends: Gecko’s ConvolverNodeEngine counts
the output it still owes in mRemainingLeftOutput, and reports itself
active through IsActive() until then. Blink’s ConvolverHandler::
RequiresTailProcessing() and TailTime() keep its handler in
DeferredTaskHandler’s tail-processing list, and WebKit’s ConvolverNode
uses requiresTailProcessing() and tailTime() the same way.
